WEBVTT

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.280
Can I ask you to take this tale--

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:40.120
the tale of Sherlock Holmes's nemesis,
the Lord of Crime, James Moriarty--

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:42.660
and bring it to a close?

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.370
Of course.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.380
What's that?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.590
The final location and time.

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.600
Also, another place is indicated which
will provide hints toward further answers.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.270
Liam...

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.400
...why did you pick me?

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.740
My role was nothing more than being the
detective who solved the riddles you set up.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:22.120
Why... did that have to be me?

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.710
Because...

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.260
Time's up.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:03.040
<i>Tripped up by your twisted words</i>

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.790
<i>I can't fall asleep at night</i>

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:10.920
<i>Transfixed by your gaze</i>

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:13.960
<i>I feel your sickness inside</i>

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:18.380
<i>Injured, I break down</i>

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:21.760
<i>this never-ending punishment</i>

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:26.140
<i>I feel your sins all the time</i>

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:30.730
<i>It's inescapable, take me away</i>

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:34.320
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.450
<i>Show me a dream that will stir me awake</i>

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:42.070
<i>I don't feel your love</i>
<i>But I can give you love</i>

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:46.200
<i>Whenever I awaken, you fall apart</i>

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.290
<i>Someday... (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.630
<i>Find me (Free your mind)</i>

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:57.090
<i>Steal your heart (Free your soul)</i>

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.970
<i>Endlessly (Free your mind)</i>

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:03.760
<i>I will scream aloud</i>

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.060
"The Final Problem Act 2"

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.150
"The Final Problem Act 2"

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.150
It's an address in the slums.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:20.780
I'm fairly certain that there is
something he wishes to tell you.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.160
You should go and find out.

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.330
John, come with me.

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:30.330
No. You're the one he
delegated this to, Sherlock.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:34.500
He's... your friend, and you're
going to save him, right?

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.800
You should do whatever you think is right.

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:50.060
Albert, there's one last thing
I wanted to ask you.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.900
What is it, Colonel?

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.570
I was planning to die
together with William,

00:03:56.570 --> 00:04:00.610
to atone for the crimes
we've committed together.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:05.120
Everyone who was
assembled here felt the same.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:11.120
But he intends to take <i>our </i>crimes
upon him with his death, as well.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:16.630
Which is to say,
he's telling us to live on.

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:21.550
What are you planning to do
with your life, Albert?

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:27.180
We should do what only those
who are left behind can do.

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:31.640
Even though I cannot bear the cross
with him at the moment,

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:36.310
I can take it up afterward
as much as needed.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:41.030
Take up his cross, huh?

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.010
Once the devils are cast out,
people's hearts become clear again,

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:05.340
and the curse is lifted.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:09.760
The country will assuredly be beautiful.

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:17.770
You are a nobleman; wouldn't you
like to see something like that?

00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:26.110
With those words... you intended to show
me a new world right from the start.

00:05:26.110 --> 00:05:30.990
By which I mean, the plan has
not been altered one whit.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:38.500
William, my dear brother, you anticipated
this outcome from the beginning.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.340
Fire!

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.630
The Lord of Crime is setting fires!

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:48.180
The Lord of Crime?!

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:50.640
Nobody lives in those buildings!

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.320
I have been expecting you.

00:06:05.940 --> 00:06:07.650
What's this?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.240
Blueprints for the <i>Noahtic</i>...

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.160
...and over here, instructions
to Hope on how to break in...

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:20.670
These are all criminal plans drawn up
by Master William. And this...

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:24.130
I was told to give this to you.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.470
Dear Sherlock Holmes,

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:39.440
let me first express my thanks
to you for making your way here.

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:41.020
As you are aware,

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:45.150
my aim is to assume all of the
responsibility for this plan onto myself.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:49.070
It is my firm belief
that through this plan,

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:53.660
the hearts of the citizens of this country
will change, slowly but surely.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:57.160
I will not personally be able
to see where this will lead,

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:04.210
but I would like to ask a favour of none
other than you, Sherlock Holmes.

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.380
Amidst this great upheaval,

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.550
there are certain to be the hushed
voices of those seeking help.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.180
I would ask that you please help them.

00:07:21.730 --> 00:07:26.780
There is one other thing.
When I came to call on you,

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.740
you probably posed the following question:

00:07:29.740 --> 00:07:32.950
Why did I choose you?

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:36.910
It would be difficult to detail
the reasons in a few brief words,

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:39.750
but I found our meeting
to be enjoyable enough

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:45.460
to forget all about my
heinous plan for a moment.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:50.630
It felt as though I had found the one
person who could understand me.

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:52.930
If it weren't for our
respective positions,

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:56.260
I should have liked to converse
with you at great length.

00:07:56.260 --> 00:08:02.730
For some reason, I have considered you
to be a long-standing friend.

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:06.520
That is why I want you at my side
when I meet my end.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:12.320
That is the reason why,
for me, it must be you.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:18.330
If only... If only we could be
reborn into a different world,

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:23.420
then this next time, I would hope
to be true friends with you.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:29.550
Likewise.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.680
I've felt the same way,
all this time, you know...

00:08:33.680 --> 00:08:35.510
You bloody imbecile!

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:47.860
The city is burning.

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:52.070
Apparently, the Lord of Crime
is setting fires all over.

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:53.860
The Lord of Crime?

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.410
There is nothing to worry about.
All of the fires are happening in the slums.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:00.080
The slums, eh?

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:03.960
The Lord of Crime has been treating
us noblemen as his sworn enemy,

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:07.670
but surprisingly enough, he appears
to be a man of egalitarian ideology.

00:09:08.790 --> 00:09:10.380
Lord Townsend!

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:15.630
What do you lot want?!

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:21.310
Lord Townsend, the fires are coming!
Please allow us to use your loading dock!

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:24.310
There are aristocratic mansions
surrounding this area,

00:09:24.310 --> 00:09:26.900
and no place to draw water from the river!

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.440
If we can carry water from
the mansion's loading dock,

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:33.360
it will be the closest distance for us
to put out the fires! Please!

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:37.740
Off with you! There is no way
I am letting you rabble in here!

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:39.240
But, sir...

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:42.370
Stop pestering me!
If you do not leave this instant,

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:46.250
then you can consider yourselves
without jobs tomorrow!

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.630
The fires are getting closer!

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:57.130
Lord Townsend, we beg you!

00:09:57.130 --> 00:09:59.680
Please, please open the gate!

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:03.430
At this rate, we'll all be--
The city of London will be--!

00:10:04.890 --> 00:10:07.190
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:12.940
Exactly what you see. We have to open
this up in order to get to the water.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:18.660
Did you not hear me?! I will not allow
you in here! Somebody stop him!

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.330
Which of us is not listening?

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:25.790
The city is burning, and the people
are here asking for help.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:28.790
If you leave things as they are,
everything will burn to ash,

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:32.040
and one way or another,
this country is finished.

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.420
"Noblesse oblige"--

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:37.630
the nobility have a mandatory obligation.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:40.680
Between those of us who are risking
our lives to put out the fires,

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:47.060
and those of you, who are doing nothing,
which of us are the true nobility?

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:52.650
Silence! We who bear highborn blood
are the nobility! All of you are--

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:58.610
Then let me ask you...
were your ancestors born nobility?

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:00.570
No, they weren't.

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:04.490
They became noble because they
gave everything for this country.

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.370
Giving all for one's country differs,

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:10.040
based on one's position
and what they have to offer.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:15.170
On how they think, how they act,
and how they accept responsibility.

00:11:15.170 --> 00:11:18.550
Weren't noblemen originally
counted not by their birth,

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:24.390
nor by their class, but by being willing
to sacrifice for their country?

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:37.030
Keep those buckets coming!

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.930
We somehow got it under control.

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.970
It's a miracle.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:14.940
Things are proceeding according
to your plan, William.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.520
All that remains...

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:31.830
Wh-What was that light just now?

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.750
It's the Tower Bridge!

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.920
Isn't that...?

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:39.460
Sherlock Holmes!

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:43.300
The other one is Moriarty,
the Lord of Crime!

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.680
Holmes has cornered the Lord of Crime!

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:52.560
I'm glad that you arrived
on time, Sherlock.

00:12:52.560 --> 00:12:56.020
So this was your plan, was it?

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:58.190
To use the fires to make the nobility

00:12:58.190 --> 00:13:02.950
and the townsfolk overcome the
class barrier and defend their city.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:09.370
Then, to have all of the negative feelings
in London focused on you.

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:14.670
The people all consider you
to be a devil, Liam.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:18.630
But there is still time.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:23.970
There isn't a single thing in this world
that can't be undone!

00:13:29.680 --> 00:13:35.890
This is how you are trying
to tempt me to cling to life...

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:41.730
<i>You </i>are the devil, Sherlock!

00:13:47.490 --> 00:13:51.080
Louis, are you sure you want to be here?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:56.750
I asked Holmes to see to Brother.
To save his life.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:01.880
I am only here to see things through--
the conclusion for those two.

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:07.090
I gave my life up for Brother
and his ideals.

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:10.720
Even knowing that his death was
assured in the distant future,

00:14:10.720 --> 00:14:13.930
I did not mind, as long as
we could die together.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:20.110
But then Brother chose to die alone.

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:25.360
I was afraid to be left
behind in this world.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:28.990
I thought that there would be
no point in living.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:33.330
I thought that I had nothing
of intrinsic value.

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:40.630
But then Brother affirmed
my existence all this time...

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.460
...assuring me that I did deserve
to be in this world.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:48.550
So no matter what conclusion
is reached here,

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:51.760
I will live and see things
through in this world.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:58.480
If anyone--any single person could
acknowledge my existence,

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.190
then I was able go on living.

00:15:01.190 --> 00:15:04.480
And if he is that someone for Brother,

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:09.150
the same way Brother has been
for me, then I'm sure...

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.660
That's enough.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:17.080
Everyone has seen the sight of the
detective fighting the Lord of Crime.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:18.500
So I'm ready...

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.960
You expect me to just stand by and
watch as you go to your death?

00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:25.210
Is dying the atonement that you've
come up with for yourself?

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:29.880
You're just doing it to escape
from your own suffering.

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:32.760
Don't use death as your escape!

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:37.180
If you truly want to atone,
then make the harder choice for yourself!

00:15:37.180 --> 00:15:41.480
Live, and atone with your life
for what you've done.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:46.070
Right? Isn't that right, Liam?

00:16:07.300 --> 00:16:09.050
You stubborn jackass!

00:16:16.890 --> 00:16:20.930
Why... would you go so far to save me?

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:26.440
Isn't that evident?
Because you are my dear friend.

00:16:28.980 --> 00:16:32.320
Living may hold nothing
but bitterness for you,

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:37.450
but the world that you are changing
is going to be a world worth living in.

00:16:37.450 --> 00:16:38.990
I'm sure of it!

00:16:38.990 --> 00:16:42.710
You can see that same future for yourself!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:46.000
So... live!

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:49.250
Live, Liam!

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.590
You...

00:16:53.590 --> 00:17:00.720
You came here not as a detective...
but as a friend, didn't you?

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.350
You've bested me, Sherly.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:18.830
I'm not about... to let you be
the only one who dies!

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:42.100
Liam, let's live.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:46.270
We both... have to live.

00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:05.580
Three months have now passed.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:09.630
Albert has relinquished his fortune
to begin a recovery fund,

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.300
whilst keeping the
Moriarty name out of it.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:18.090
Word is that many other aristocrats
have contributed to it, as well.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:21.760
Despite having a large-scale
search effort made,

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:25.730
William's body was never located.

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:30.940
However, I...

00:18:30.940 --> 00:18:34.110
Thank you for coming, Louis.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.950
Is this...?

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:42.200
Yes. All of the incidents up to now
have been collected in story form.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.200
It should be going on sale before long,

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:47.830
and I received a volume
from its author, Dr Watson.

00:18:49.670 --> 00:18:54.960
You need not worry. The book's content
portrays Professor Moriarty

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:58.340
as an evil figure of
unprecedented proportions.

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:05.350
Then Mr Watson penned this with
full knowledge of what transpired.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:11.360
I offer my heartfelt gratitude

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:17.070
for you three brothers staking your
lives for the sake of Great Britain.

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.910
The secret arrangement my brother
pushed on the House of Lords,

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:24.030
demanding that they abolish their
superiority over the House of Commons,

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:27.290
is a deal that could only be made
because of your plan.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:32.840
Now, the Moriarty family
joins the Holmes family

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:40.340
as one that must bear their crime and
punishment toward Britain in perpetuity.

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:48.520
Yes. I-- <i>We </i>now live to pay for our crimes.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:55.770
I am the one who asked my brother
William to carry out the plan.

00:19:55.770 --> 00:20:01.660
The entire blame for this lies with me,
Albert James Moriarty.

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:04.370
I am prepared to accept the punishment

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:07.290
and answer for these crimes
in William's place.

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:13.380
There are many different ways
to take responsibility,

00:20:13.380 --> 00:20:16.130
but I thought it very much like him

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:20.010
to impose even greater punishment
on himself. Furthermore...

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:27.720
...he is not alone in living his life in service
to his country to answer for his crimes.

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:30.770
Louis, are you certain about this?

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:34.860
Yes. My determination remains unchanged.

00:20:34.860 --> 00:20:37.070
Very well.

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:42.610
Louis James Moriarty,
I hereby commit to you...

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:45.950
...the newly-created Section 6,
charged with protecting this reborn Britain,

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:51.660
one which does not officially exist,
and answers directly to Her Majesty--

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.040
MI6.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:02.050
I believe that William is still alive.
Which is why...

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:08.640
...I must preserve this beautiful world
that Brother has created.

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:12.100
That is my mission.

00:21:31.950 --> 00:21:33.540
Welcome.

00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:36.790
Scotch.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:40.960
Sir, this is Switzerland.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:44.590
This is kirsch. Give it a try.

00:21:47.010 --> 00:21:50.350
I doubt you're this far into
the countryside on business.

00:21:50.350 --> 00:21:53.560
Are you out here chasing after a woman?

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:56.810
Nope. I'm looking for a friend.

00:21:56.810 --> 00:21:59.520
What sort of friend?

00:21:59.520 --> 00:22:02.440
Well, let's see...

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:08.450
One that would look up at a spiral staircase
and check for the golden ratio.

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:10.580
That sort of friend.

00:22:15.960 --> 00:22:20.750
Catch me if you can, Mr Holmes.

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:29.760
<i>Fate that over time changes</i>
<i>into chains of sorrow,</i>

00:22:29.760 --> 00:22:37.980
<i>leave me the light of rebirth</i>
<i>for the world ahead</i>

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:48.570
<i>Struck by a frustration</i>
<i>I'd never experienced before,</i>

00:22:48.570 --> 00:22:51.950
<i>I feel lost, I feel lost</i>

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:55.950
<i>The letters I dashed off</i>
<i>are all I remember</i>

00:22:55.950 --> 00:22:59.330
<i>It's all true, it's all true</i>

00:22:59.330 --> 00:23:06.760
<i>Witness as I forgo my forsaken future</i>
<i>with no regrets</i>

00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:15.350
<i>and you will win your intent</i>
<i>at the expense of becoming my pawn</i>

00:23:17.350 --> 00:23:23.150
<i>A scarlet thread fluttering in the wind</i>
<i>at five in the morning</i>

00:23:23.150 --> 00:23:29.400
<i>I'll recover my memories on the last day</i>

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:32.200
<i>Hold me down till the end</i>

00:23:32.200 --> 00:23:37.870
<i>Finish by wiping away my sins,</i>

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:44.550
<i>warning me to stay true if I desire beauty</i>
